  "rationale": "The representative target scissors has almost no probability after “The red”: its current output root has adjective-conditioned rules tied to a preceding verb, but lacks a general rule for a noun following an adjective. Add a moderate suffix-adjective rule for scissors, consistent with the batch’s repeated adjective-plus-noun phrases, without asserting which noun is certain. Several batch examples also place a proper name after an introductory comma. A suffix-comma rule raises the proper-name class across names rather than memorizing a person or story. Commas can introduce other continuations, and adjectives do not determine a unique noun, so these additions preserve alternatives rather than treating either pattern as mandatory.",
